  {
    "pkattachmentId": 76442,
    "bookid": 72,
    "chapterId": 199,
    "fileId": 50119,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Diagnostic algorithm for neuroendocrine neoplasm",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Neuroendocrine (NE) markers are chromogranin&nbsp;A, synaptophysin, and INSM1. Mixed neuroendocrine&ndash;non-neuroendocrine neoplasm (MiNEN) and amphicrine-like carcinoma are classification categories and not specific diagnoses. NEC, neuroendocrine carcinoma (i.e. poorly differentiated neuroendocrine neoplasm); NEN, neuroendocrine neoplasm; NET, neuroendocrine tumour (i.e. well-differentiated neuroendocrine neoplasm). Notes: (1)&nbsp;Positive for at least two of the three markers tested. (2)&nbsp;Defined as &ge;&nbsp;70%. (3)&nbsp;Minor subpopulation of conventional cancer allowed. (4)&nbsp;30% rule exception: when the NEN component is made by small cell NEC, any percentage subpopulation should be reported.",
    "source": "The Editors team.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/199/50119.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/199/thumb_50119.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 76450,
    "bookid": 72,
    "chapterId": 199,
    "fileId": 50148,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Non-pure neuroendocrine neoplasm types",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Neuroendocrine neoplasms (NEN) when not composed exclusively (&gt;&nbsp;70%) of neuroendocrine cells may present as mixed neuroendocrine&ndash;non-neuroendocrine neoplasms (MiNEN) with two morphologically separate elements or as amphicrine-like carcinoma with morphologically undistinguishable components either composed by cells with the capacity of dual secretion (exocrine and neuroendocrine) and/or by separate neuroendocrine and non-neuroendocrine cells as indistinguishable populations. Light-yellow cells with small granules represent neuroendocrine cells; light-blue cells with large white granules represent exocrine cells; light-blue cells (exocrine) with yellow granules (neuroendocrine) represent amphicrine cells.",
    "source": "",
